iMac 5K dual-tile panel: half-dark panel at the disk-encryption password prompt.

Applies on top of imac5k-amdgpu-7.2.2.patch. Confirmed on hardware.

Half-dark panel at the disk-encryption password prompt
   The slave tile only gets a DC stream during an atomic modeset (see the
   stitch block in amdgpu_dm_atomic_check), and drm_client_setup()'s
   initial fbdev config deliberately stops short of committing one: it
   probes, sets up the crtcs and calls register_framebuffer(), leaving the
   commit to a later hotplug or to fbcon taking over the console. With
   "quiet splash" fbcon defers take-over, so on this machine that first
   commit landed 1.16 s after fb0 went live (5.911 s -> 7.069 s in the boot
   log). For that whole window the panel presents the full-width stitched
   mode while only the root tile scans out, and the right-hand half is
   dark -- long enough to cover the password prompt.

   Fix: once fbdev is set up, if this device drives a stitched tile panel,
   issue a second client hotplug. That takes the dev->fb_helper path, which
   does commit, so the peer tile stream is created during probe instead of
   whenever something else happens to trigger a modeset. Confirmed on
   hardware: peer stream added 3 ms after fb0, down from 1160 ms.

No-op on hardware without the tiled-panel quirk.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
